Janis Papanagnou wrote:
>
> I seem to recall that it was said that effectiveness of attack spells
> like magic missile would increase if the characters experience level
> increases.

Failure rate falls and damage done increases.  Wizard charaters will
usually want to go all the way to XP=30 because of this.

> Ah, and I forgot; my wizard has the option to enhance a couple of spell
> schools from Basic to Skilled. I know that difficult high-level spells
> will become available by skill enhancement, but since all I have are the
> level 1 and 2 attack spells that doesn't really matter much. But would
> the attack spell's damage increase as well with better skill? (I suspect
> not, but don't know.)

Specific attack spells change at skilled - Fireball cone of cold go from
a ray to a blast centered on a location.  Because of the wide zone of
damage you may want to enhance to skilled.  Because you have to be able
to see the target square you may not want to enhance to skilled.  You
have the skill slots either way so it's a decision to make.

Others have posted that damage from magic missile goes with XP not
skill.  I'll add that MR makes you immune to magic missiles and some
monsters are immune.  You'll want to have more attack spells than magic
missile.

With a wizard I almost always want as many XP levels as possible because
of the damage.  At each level I also consider what to spend the skill
slot on.  I have an extensive write-up on wizard skill slots.  It was my
first one so it's verbose.  In it I note that at XP=30 there are enough
skill slots to enhance *all* spell schools, but dagger to Expert, plus
if you get Stormy/Vorpy broad/long-sword, and have 3 slots left over. 
What I'll spend those on vary game to game.  Sometimes I need to burn
them on quarterstaff for survival.  Sometimes I burn them on polearm
(spetum) for fun at the castle gates.  Sometimes I spend them on
artifacts as they arrive.

Once you're at 0% failure for some spell it's no longer worth enhancing
further except those spells that change behavior at skilled.  Because of
fireball and cone of cold attack might not be advanced to keep them
rays.

Robes improve spell success.  A wizard tends to hit 0% failure on all
spells before XP=30 without a robe.  In the end robes are for classes
other than wizards to me.


